# Pinned counts for scripts/gate_published_consistency.sh — a RATCHET, not a pass mark.
#
# These are KNOWN-OPEN defects, not acceptable ones. The gate fails if a count RISES, and tells you
# to tighten the pin if a count FALLS. The point is that a published-consistency defect can no longer
# be introduced silently; the standing ones stay visible instead of being waved through by a gate
# that prints FAIL on every push and is therefore read by nobody.
#
# Recorded 2026-09-06. Re-pin in the SAME commit as any change that legitimately moves a count.
#
# G1 — unfilled placeholders in published reports.
#      5: [REPRO-TAG] x2 (a git tag minted at TR-12 publication; it cannot be filled before the
#      freeze) and [EXPECTED-Q1|Q9|XA] x3 (filled by the n=31 battery's expected-output blocks,
#      which do not exist until that run happens).
G1=5
# G2 — published --estimate-knuth commands with no thread pin.
#      10: NOT fixable by adding a number. Measured 2026-09-06: 45 files under reports/evidence/
#      carry a threads= header, so the counts exist, but the mapping from a PUBLISHED FIGURE to the
#      RUN that produced it is not recorded. TR7_CIRCULAR_READING.md:158 has six candidate evidence
#      files matching its probe count and nothing says which one produced the published figures.
#      Adding a pin would FABRICATE provenance, which is worse than the gap. The real defect is one
#      level up: a published command does not name the artifact it reproduces.
G2=10
# G3 — published disclosures that have gone stale. Shaped to fire when the artifact EXISTS.
G3=0
